<title>RUSSIA: RUSSIA 364-DAY T-BILL YIELDS 19.11 PCT - C. BANK.</title>
<headline>RUSSIA 364-DAY T-BILL YIELDS 19.11 PCT - C. BANK.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 364-day Russian GKO discount Treasury bills was 19.11 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the central bank said.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the average yield between 18.93 and 19.17 percent.</p>
<p>Series 21083 bills, maturing on August 5, 1998 and the closest maturity date to the new issue, closed at 84.97 on Tuesday to yield 19.03 percent.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number		  21085</p>
<p>    Issue volume		   7.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		  1.00 million rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		 8.08 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Bids (cash)		    6.75 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Sold			     5.94 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Proceeds			 4.99 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Average price		  83.99 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	83.88 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		  19.11 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield     19.27 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			    364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		  Aug 12, 1998</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the Finance Ministry will offer 4.50 trillion roubles in an issue of 182-day T-bills (series 21084).</p>
<p>It will also repay about 8.36 trillion roubles ($1.4 billion) 252-day T-bills (series 22061).</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
<p>($ = 5804 Russian Roubles)</p>
